    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0858" n="848" xml:id="pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.6336/12–2248: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-22T11:00:00+03:00">December 22,
                            1948—11 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 22—8:45 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2989. As telegraph and post offices report transmission telegrams and letters
                    Mukden impossible, Embassy is trying to secure report and arrange communications
                    through Foreign Office as suggested Deptel 1358, December 2.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Dairen 31, Nanking 54.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
